  <adoption-note date="2026-08-28">
    ADOPTED INTO THIS PROJECT, NOT DEFERRED. Owner direction 2026-08-28: "if an issue is
    important, then it should be added to this project NOT deferred to others."

    The failing job is `Full Unit Tests (Debug)` in ci-tier2-advisory.yml, a workflow THIS PROJECT created. The suite was ALWAYS failing; the aggregator masked every result to `pass` until PR #840 repaired it. A tier this project built, reporting failures this project introduced the reporting for.

    This is a DEFECT REPORT AGAINST THIS PROJECT OWN DELIVERABLE, not new scope. The project
    cannot honestly close while something it shipped is known-broken. That is north star #1
    ("fix it right the first time") and #3 ("no constant reds").
  </adoption-note>

  <goal>The 5 real-clock timing tests pass deterministically in CI, and no test in the touched set uses Stopwatch, DateTime.UtcNow or Task.Delay for a timing assertion.</goal>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Identify the 5 from run 33131511758, job `Full Unit Tests (Debug)`. Start with RetryAndIdempotencyTests.CancellationDuringRetryLoop_StopsImmediately.</step>
    <step order="2">For each, confirm the failure is real-clock sensitivity and not a genuine defect. A loaded shared runner is the trigger; passing locally is NOT evidence of correctness.</step>
    <step order="3">Convert to FakeTimeProvider per tests/CLAUDE.md "TimeProvider over Stopwatch". Stopwatch / DateTime.UtcNow / Task.Delay are BANNED in tests by that directive; these predate it.</step>
    <step order="4">Re-run the Tier 2 unit job. Confirm green AND confirm runtime did not regress: these tests currently WAIT on real clocks, so FakeTimeProvider should make them faster, not slower.</step>
  </steps>

  <notes date="2026-08-28">
    PARTIAL — 4 of the 5 fixed. Full findings: notes/091-realclock-findings.md.

    Two premises in #848 were wrong and are corrected there:
    (1) FakeTimeProvider is NOT "referenced nowhere" (per #795) — it is already used in 16 files,
        including RetryAndIdempotencyTests itself; and ScheduledJobHost ALREADY took an optional
        TimeProvider and routed every sleep through it. The production work was done; the tests had
        simply never adopted it. This task changed ZERO production files.
    (2) ReAnalysisFlowTests.ReAnalysis_HappyPath_... is NOT a real-clock timing test. It has no
        Stopwatch, no clock, no timing assertion, and it reproduces DETERMINISTICALLY on a dev
        machine — HttpClient's 100s default timeout while the SSE path attempts a LIVE Azure Search
        call. It surfaces in a job named "Full Unit Tests" because ci-tier2-advisory.yml pass 1 is
        bare `dotnet test` with no project filter, so the whole solution (integration tests
        included) runs there. That is a real defect in this project's own deliverable.

    ESCALATED, not fixed: repairing it means editing ci-tier2-advisory.yml, and the shadow window
    forbids tier-file edits while it runs ("changing the configuration invalidates what was
    observed" — window was 6/20 PRs at the time). It is also an owner call, since filtering
    integration tests out of Tier 2 means they run nowhere on a PR. The test is advisory and
    blocks no one meanwhile. Recommendation in the findings note; sequence after cutover (071).

    ALSO FOUND, deliberately not fixed (out of scope, both documented in the findings note):
    - ScheduledJobHost.TriggerNowAsync passes CancellationToken.None to RunManualTriggerAsync while
      its own comment claims it uses the host stoppingToken — manual-trigger jobs cannot observe
      host shutdown, so StopAsync waits out the full drain timeout. Latent NFR-07 gap, no coverage.
    - TickAsync refreshes before the due-check and recomputes NextFireUtc from `now` EXCLUSIVE, so
      RefreshInterval shorter than the cron period starves dispatch under jitter-free timing. Real
      deployments escape it only via sleep jitter.
  </notes>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Tier 2 `Full Unit Tests (Debug)` reports 0 failures</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No Stopwatch / Task.Delay / DateTime.UtcNow remains in the touched tests</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tier 2 p95 still within the NFR-02 8-minute budget</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
